# Test safety

Default backend tests are hermetic. Credentials existing locally do not imply permission.

Without explicit `ARENA_INTEGRATION_TESTS=1`, tests must not reach:

- Appwrite
- Neon
- Modal
- provider APIs
- Vercel mutation

## Default command

```text
backend/.venv/bin/python -m pytest --ignore=tests/evals
```

`pytest.ini` already deselects `modal`, `integration`, `postgres`, and `provider_eval`. Keep `--ignore=tests/evals` (DeepEval imports OpenRouter at collection).

Real Postgres additionally needs `ARENA_PG_TEST_URL`. Do not claim application test hardening beyond `hermetic.py`, `conftest.py`, and those markers.

## Claims

Treat "exactly once", "concurrency safe", "isolated", "authoritative", "hidden", and "hermetic" as unproven until tests and code agree. Prefer real DB sessions over process-local locks. `test-debugger` is readonly.
